\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Design family used in the paper. The packet-isolated subgroup shares the same source model, the same handoff latch, and the same measurement hooks; this is what makes the same-family ablations informative. The \textsc  {Confidence-Gated}conductance range comes from the implemented term $G_{\mathrm  {scout}} + G_{\mathrm  {conf}}(0.25 + 0.75m(t))$ with $G_{\mathrm  {scout}}=\SI {40}{\nano \siemens }$, $G_{\mathrm  {conf}}=\SI {8}{\nano \siemens }$, and commit signal $m(t)\in [0,1]$.\relax }}{7}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:designs}{{2}{7}{Design family used in the paper. The packet-isolated subgroup shares the same source model, the same handoff latch, and the same measurement hooks; this is what makes the same-family ablations informative. The \Confidence conductance range comes from the implemented term $G_{\mathrm {scout}} + G_{\mathrm {conf}}(0.25 + 0.75m(t))$ with $G_{\mathrm {scout}}=\SI {40}{\nano \siemens }$, $G_{\mathrm {conf}}=\SI {8}{\nano \siemens }$, and commit signal $m(t)\in [0,1]$.\relax }{table.caption.3}{}}
